`resolve_native_path` returns `current_exe()` directly when invoked with an explicit path. If `env::current_exe()` fails on a platform/environment (it can return `io::Error`), `starship init ...` will now fail even though a PATH lookup could have succeeded. Consider falling back when `current_exe()` errors in this branch (e.g., try `current_exe().or_else(|_| lookup_path())`, or fall back to `argv0`/a resolved form of it) to avoid introducing a new hard failure mode for explicit-path invocations.
